.TH diskviz "1" "" "The scalpel3 Disk Visualizer" "The scalpel3 Disk Visualizer"

.SH NAME
diskviz \- Visualize synthetic disk image layouts

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diskviz
\fIkeyfile\fR
[\fB-d\fR \fIbasedir\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBdiskviz\fR reads a \fI.key\fR file produced by \fBfragmentator\fR(1) and renders an interactive GUI visualization of the disk image layout using SDL2.
.PP
In block views, each disk block is a cell in a grid. Image files (PNG, JPG,
GIF) are rendered as tiled image blocks showing the actual image content.
Other file types are shown as colored labeled blocks. RANDOM fill blocks
appear as colorful noise and ZERO fill blocks display "0" characters.
.PP
The tool has eight views. The first four illustrate files, filesystem block
mapping, data remaining after filesystem information is lost, and header/footer
locations for a contiguous layout. The next four illustrate the corresponding
fragmented layout. It starts at the first view. These are illustrations based
on the key file, not a display of scalpel3 recovery progress.

.SH OPTIONS
.PP
.TP
.BI -d " basedir"
Base directory for resolving file paths referenced in the key file. If not specified, paths are resolved relative to the current working directory.

.SH INTERACTION
.PP
.TP
.B SPACEBAR / RIGHT ARROW
Advance to the next view, stopping at view 8.
.TP
.B LEFT ARROW
Return to the previous view, stopping at view 1.
.TP
.B 1-8
Jump directly to the corresponding view.
.TP
.B + / - / 0
Zoom in, zoom out, or reset zoom in the block views (3, 4, 7, and 8).
.TP
.B Mouse wheel
Scroll vertically in a block view.
.TP
.B Q / ESC
Quit the application. Keyboard controls work from both the terminal and the
graphical window.
.TP
.B Mouse hover
In block views, hover over a block to see its file and block information.
.TP
.B Window resize
The grid automatically recomputes to fill the window.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fragmentator (1),
.BR scalpel3 (1)

